{"entryId":"1234","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1234:1","sourceSha256":"9e9fb882d2d77825f9501f0c662b222dc7bd35184aa868dd84faaa4ae82a0f93","englishSha256":"dbcaaedaa5c9a40c8cc12ef183769a4e980321117020d2c141f114682420b7d7","citations":[{"id":"1234:1:citation-01","he":[23,39],"en":[30,53],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Midrash_Tehillim_62.3"},"reference":"Midrash Tehillim 62:3","assessment":"The checked Shocher Tov variant names Chiyya bar Abba, explicitly from Yaffo. Keep Heilprin’s Adda heading and record the witness difference.","evidence":[{"reference":"Midrash Tehillim 62:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Midrash_Tehillim_62.3"},"witness":"OYW"}]},{"id":"1234:1:citation-02","he":[40,53],"en":[55,88],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Vayikra_Rabbah_33.6"},"reference":"Vayikra Rabbah 33:6","assessment":"The checked Vayikra Rabbah reads Chiyya son of Rabbi Adda of Yaffo.","evidence":[{"reference":"Vayikra Rabbah 33:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Vayikra_Rabbah_33.6"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]},{"id":"1234:1:citation-03","he":[54,63],"en":[90,117],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bereshit_Rabbah_38.13"},"reference":"Bereshit Rabbah 38:13","assessment":"Bereshit Rabbah calls Chiyya the son of Rav Adda’s son, of Yaffo. This is a distinct generational formulation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bereshit Rabbah 38:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bereshit_Rabbah_38.13"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]},{"id":"1234:1:citation-04","he":[65,88],"en":[123,161],"target":{"url":"https://yitzchoklowy.com/text/midrash/shir-hashirim-rabbah/parasha-8/"},"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 8:12, Vatican 76 transcription","assessment":"The Chazit passage is under Song 8:12. The transcription of Vatican 76 reads Adda of Yaffo and the edition’s apparatus reports Abba in Vilna.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 8:12, Vatican 76 transcription","target":{"url":"https://yitzchoklowy.com/text/midrash/shir-hashirim-rabbah/parasha-8/"},"witness":"Vatican 76 transcription with Vilna variant apparatus"}]},{"id":"1234:1:citation-05","he":[90,138],"en":[162,203],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Moed_Katan_3.7.14"},"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Moed Katan 3:7:14","assessment":"Rif cites the same torn-garment statement as Chiyya bar Abba of Yaffo, while the Yerushalmi witness gives Adda.","evidence":[{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Moed Katan 3:7:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Moed_Katan_3.7.14"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"},{"reference":"Rif Megillah 15a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rif_Megillah_15a.8"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1234:1:citation-06","he":[140,196],"en":[237,278],"target":{"url":"https://daat.ac.il/daat/toshba/yerushalmi/moed/yeru-megila.pdf"},"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Megillah, Vilna 27a","assessment":"The Vilna-based text on folio 27a explicitly gives son of Adda of Yaffo jointly with Yirmiyah in Zeira’s name. Soferim shares that chain. The Bavli assigns the one-breath instruction directly to Rav Adda of Yaffo.","evidence":[{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Megillah, Vilna 27a","target":{"url":"https://daat.ac.il/daat/toshba/yerushalmi/moed/yeru-megila.pdf"},"witness":"Daat Vilna-based Yerushalmi on Megillah"},{"reference":"Megillah 16b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah_16b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,5],"holds":[{"raw":"שוחר טוב סי' ס\"ב ומ\"ר בהר פל\"ג וב\"ר פל\"ח","reason":"The checked texts give Abba, son of Adda and grandson of Adda, respectively. Preserve different kinship formulations.","evidence":[{"reference":"Midrash Tehillim 62:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Midrash_Tehillim_62.3"},"witness":"OYW"},{"reference":"Vayikra Rabbah 33:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Vayikra_Rabbah_33.6"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"},{"reference":"Bereshit Rabbah 38:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bereshit_Rabbah_38.13"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]},{"raw":"ובחזית פ' כרמי שלי לפני","reason":"The Vatican transcription has son of Adda and its apparatus reports son of Abba in Vilna.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 8:12, Vatican 76 transcription","target":{"url":"https://yitzchoklowy.com/text/midrash/shir-hashirim-rabbah/parasha-8/"},"witness":"Vatican 76 transcription with Vilna variant apparatus"}]},{"raw":"בריה דרב אדא דמן יפו","reason":"The checked Yerushalmi has Adda, and Rif gives Abba in the same torn-garment discussion.","evidence":[{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Moed Katan 3:7:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Moed_Katan_3.7.14"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"},{"reference":"Rif Megillah 15a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rif_Megillah_15a.8"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"raw":"ברי' דר' אדא דיפו בש\"ר זעירא","reason":"Vilna and Soferim include Yirmiyah in the transmission. Bavli gives a separate form naming Adda of Yaffo directly.","evidence":[{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Megillah, Vilna 27a","target":{"url":"https://daat.ac.il/daat/toshba/yerushalmi/moed/yeru-megila.pdf"},"witness":"Daat Vilna-based Yerushalmi on Megillah"},{"reference":"Tractate Soferim 13:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tractate_Soferim_13.5"},"witness":"Talmud Bavli, Vilna 1883 ed."},{"reference":"Megillah 16b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah_16b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The Yaffo witnesses differ in patronymic and generation. The Chazit comparison is from the Vatican 76 transcription with named Vilna variant. The Vilna-based Yerushalmi gives Yirmiyah with Chiyya in Zeira’s name.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Tractate Soferim 13:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tractate_Soferim_13.5"},"witness":"Talmud Bavli, Vilna 1883 ed."},{"reference":"Midrash Tehillim 62:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Midrash_Tehillim_62.3"},"witness":"OYW"},{"reference":"Vayikra Rabbah 33:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Vayikra_Rabbah_33.6"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"},{"reference":"Bereshit Rabbah 38:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bereshit_Rabbah_38.13"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Moed Katan 3:7:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Moed_Katan_3.7.14"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"},{"reference":"Rif Megillah 15a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rif_Megillah_15a.8"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 8:12, Vatican 76 transcription","target":{"url":"https://yitzchoklowy.com/text/midrash/shir-hashirim-rabbah/parasha-8/"},"witness":"Vatican 76 transcription with Vilna variant apparatus"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Megillah, Vilna 27a","target":{"url":"https://daat.ac.il/daat/toshba/yerushalmi/moed/yeru-megila.pdf"},"witness":"Daat Vilna-based Yerushalmi on Megillah"},{"reference":"Megillah 16b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah_16b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
